; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6592    MD_CanTp_2003
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6593      Description: Rule 15.2: An unconditional break statement shall terminate every non-empty switch clause.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6594      Reason:      The break statement of the previous case is intentionally omitted to avoid doubled code (fall-though).
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6595      Risk:        none
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6596      Prevention:  N/A
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6597  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6598    MD_CanTp_ReturnPaths:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6599      Reason:      More than one return statement for better readability (e.g. less if-nesting).
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6600      Risk:        None
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6601      Prevention:  N/A
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6602  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6603    MD_CanTp_3333:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6604      Description: Rule 14.6: A break statement is being used to exit from a switch case block but is not the final statement in the block.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6605      Reason:      break statement that is not at the end of a case block is used for a better readability and less resource consumption.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6606      Risk:        none
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6607      Prevention:  N/A
