; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6765  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_RXSTATE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6766    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpRxState pointer is used in an internal function for write access. It is passed to this function
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6767                    as a parameter and expected to valid. Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6768    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6769  
