; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6774  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6775  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_TXSTATE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6776    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpTxState pointer is in an internal function for write access and/or as parameter to another
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6777                    function. It passed to this function as a parameter and expected to valid.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6778                    Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6779    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6780  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6781  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_CALL_TXSTATE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6782    \DESCRIPTION    The pTpTxState pointer is used in an internal function as parameter to another function. It is passed to
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6783                    this function as a parameter and expected to valid. Pointer validity is analyzed at the function call.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6784    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6785  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6786  \ID SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_CALCBS
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6787    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to the CanTp_CalcBS array, indexed by the RxHdl. RxHdl is part of the struct referenced
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6788                    by the pTpRxState pointer, which is a function parameter here and expected to refer to a valid and
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6789                    initialized channel state. This implies that RxHdl is < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxHdls, which is mapped to
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6790                    CanTp_GetSizeOfRxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6791                    The CanTp_CalcBS array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_RxSduCfg.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6792    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXARRAYSIZES]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6793  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6794  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TASK_WRITE_RXSTATE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6795    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_MainFunctionRx, the pTpRxState pointer is used for write access. It is initialized to the RxState
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6796                    array, indexed by lRxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0 and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxChannels-1).
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6797                    CanTp_Cfg_GetNumRxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfRxState in CanTp_Priv.h.
