; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6808                    array, indexed by lTxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0 and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels-1).
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6809                    CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxState in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6810    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6811  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6812  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TASK_CALL_TXSTATE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6813    \DESCRIPTION    In CanTp_MainFunctionTx, the pTpTxState pointer is used as function parameter to other internal functions.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6814                    The pointer is initialized before (see [SBSW_CANTP_TASK_WRITE_TXSTATE]), and it is ensured that the
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6815                    state is initialized (TxHdl != invalid).
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6816    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6817  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6818  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_WRITE_DEST
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6819    \DESCRIPTION    The pointer pDest and the upper limit for the used index (Count) are parameters of the function and expected
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6820                    to be valid and consistent.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6821    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6822  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6823  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_PAYLOAD
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6824    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy in order to copy the payload of a received frame to the RxState struct.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6825                    The parameters Dest and Count must be valid and consistent.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6826                    - pDest parameter is valid since it references the Payload array of the RxState struct. The array
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6827                      size is CANTP_MAX_PAYLOAD_LENGTH, which is generated. For the validity of pTpRxState, see
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6828                      [SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_RXSTATE]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6829                    - Count parameter pTpRxState->PayloadLength is set in different sections of the code but can never be
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6830                      larger than CanTp_RxCfg_GetMaxPayload.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6831    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_RXMAXPAYLOADLENGTH]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6832  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6833  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_FCDATA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6834    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy in order to copy a flow control frame to the TxState struct. The parameters
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6835                    pDest and Count must be valid and consistent.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6836                    - pDest parameter is valid since it references the FCData array of the TxState struct. The array size
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6837                      is 4. For validity of TxState pointer, see [SBSW_CANTP_INTERNAL_WRITE_TXSTATE].
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6838                    - Count parameter is calculated as CANTP_PCI_LENGTH_FC + lAddressingOffset, where CANTP_PCI_LENGTH_FC
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6839                      is 3 and Addressing Offset can only be 1 or 0.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6840    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6841  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6842  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_TXQUEUE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6843    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy in order to copy a CanTp frame to the TxQueue. The parameters pDest and
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6844                    Count must be valid and consistent.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6845                    - pDest parameter is valid since it references the SduData array of the CanTp_TxQueueEntryType. The
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6846                      array size is CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6847                    - Count parameter is derived from the PaddingLength and SduLength values, which are passed to
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6848                      CanTp_CanIfTransmit and are expected to be consistent with the SduDataPtr. The largest array which
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6849                      is referenced by SduDataPtr (see [SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR]) has a size of
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6850                      CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6851    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6852  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6853  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_TXFRAMEDATA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6854    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy from CanTp_TxTransmitFrame. The content of parameters pDest and Count must be valid
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6855                    and consistent. The consistency is also needed at other code locations and is justified with
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6856                    [SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR].
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6857    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6858  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6859  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_TXFRAMEMETADATA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6860    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy from CanTp_TxTransmitFrame to append metadata to a PDU. The passed pDest parameter
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6861                    (&pTpData->SduDataPtr[pTpData->SduLength]) points to the first element after the CAN frame payload. The
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6862                    passed Count parameter contains the metadata's length. The pointer pTpData->SduDataPtr must point to an
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6863                    array of length (CANTP_FRAME_FC_MAX_LENGTH + CANTP_MAX_PDU_METADATA_LENGTH) or
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6864                    (CANTP_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH + CANTP_MAX_PDU_METADATA_LENGTH).
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6865    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_MAXPDUMETADATALENGTH]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6866  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6867  \ID SBSW_CANTP_MEMCPY_CALL_TXSDUMETADATA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6868    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_Util_MemCpy from CanTp_TxTransmitFrame to store the extracted Tx SDU metadata. The passed
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6869                    pDest parameter (pTpTxState->SduMetadata) points to an array of lenght CANTP_MAX_SDU_METADATA_LENGTH.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6870                    The passed pSrc (CanTpTxInfoPtr->SduDataPtr) is assumed to be valid and forwarded unchanged. The passed
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6871                    metadata length is less than or equal to CANTP_MAX_SDU_METADATA_LENGTH, which is generated depending on
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6872                    the available addressing modes.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6873    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_MAXSDUMETADATALENGTH]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6874  
