; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6967    \DESCRIPTION    When using the TxQueue, accesses to the queue entries are encapsulated by macros. These macros return
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6968                    an element of the CanTp_TxQueue.Entries array, which is of the size CANTP_TX_QUEUE_SIZE.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6969                    The index used by the macros is either CanTp_TxQueue.ReadPos or CanTp_TxQueue.WritePos.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6970                    It have been verified by review that these values are either set to zero, or a bit masked upon
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6971                    modification is used to ensure that the value doesn't exceed the array size. The TxConfPduId used as index is also
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6972                    expected to be valid.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6973    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCFG_TXCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  6974  
