; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7077  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7078  \ID SBSW_CANTP_TXGETFREECHANNEL_WRITE_STATE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7079    \DESCRIPTION    Write access to pTpTxState pointer, which is initialized before, depending on the channel assignment:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7080                    - dynamic: pointer is set to CanTp_TxState array, indexed by lTxChannelHdl, which iterates between 0
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7081                      and (CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels-1). CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxChannels is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxState
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7082                      in CanTp_Priv.h, so lTxChannelHdl is always in range.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7083                    - static: pointer is set to CanTp_TxState array, indexed by TxHdl parameter. TxHdl is expected to
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7084                      be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxHdls, which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSduCfg in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7085                      The CanTp_TxState array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_TxSduCfg.
