; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7088  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_TPDATAPTR
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7089    \DESCRIPTION    The TpDataPtr parameter, as well as the SduDataPtr and SduLength, which are part of the referenced
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7090                    struct, are expected to be valid and consistent. The padding length from the PduTxData pointer is
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7091                    always expected to be less than or equal to the length of the buffer referenced by the SduDataPtr.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7092    \COUNTERMEASURE \N -
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7093  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7094  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_TXSEMAPHORE
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7095    \DESCRIPTION    The TxConfPduId, which is part of the struct referenced by the PduTxData pointer parameter, is used as
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7096                    array index for the CanTp_TxSemaphores and CanTp_TxQueue arrays. It is expected to be < CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus,
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7097                    which is mapped to CanTp_GetSizeOfTxSemaphores in CanTp_Priv.h.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7098                    The CanTp_TxQueue array must therefore have the same size as CanTp_TxSemaphores.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7099    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCONFARRAYSIZES]
