; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7101  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_CALL_TXDATA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7102    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_CanIfTransmitFrame for a SF, FF or CF. The following constraints given in the function
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7103                    description must be fulfilled:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7104                    - "pTpData and pTpData->SduDataPtr are valid pointers": both pointers reference local variables. -> ok
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7105                    - "pTpData->SduLength is less or equal pPduTxData->PaddingLength":
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7106                      This is guaranteed by CanTp_Util_PaddingLength, which calculates the PaddingLength. -> ok
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7107                    - "pPduTxData->PaddingLength must not exceed the size of the array referenced by pTpData->SduDataPtr":
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7108                      the consistency is also needed at other code locations and is justified with
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7109                      [see SBSW_CANTP_TXTRANSMITFRAME_WRITE_SDUDATAPTR].
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7110                    - "pPduTxData->TxConfPduId is a valid CanTp TxConfPduId (< CanTp_Cfg_GetNumTxConfPdus)":
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7111                      TxConfPduId is read from the configuration by CanTp_TxCfg_GetTxConfPduId.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7112                    - "pPduTxData->SduHdl and pPduTxData->SduDirection must refer to a valid Rx / Tx handle": SduHdl is
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7113                      set to TxHdl, which is valid in this context, and SduDirection is set to CANTP_DIR_TX accordingly.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7114    \COUNTERMEASURE \R [CM_CANTP_TXCFG_TXCONFPDUIDS]
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7115  
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7116  \ID SBSW_CANTP_CANIFTRANSMITFRAME_CALL_FCDATA
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7117    \DESCRIPTION    Call to CanTp_CanIfTransmitFrame for a flow control frame. The following constraints given in the
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7118                    function description must be fulfilled:
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7119                    - "pTpData and pTpData->SduDataPtr are valid pointers": both pointers reference local variables. -> ok
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7120                    - "pTpData->SduLength is less or equal pPduTxData->PaddingLength":
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7121                      This is guaranteed by CanTp_Util_PaddingLength, which calculates the padding length. -> ok
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7122                    - "pPduTxData->PaddingLength must not exceed the size of the array referenced by pTpData->SduDataPtr":
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7123                      SduDataPtr reference lFCBuffer, which is of size CANTP_FRAME_FC_MAX_LENGTH. This can be 4 or 8,
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7124                      depending on padding activation.
; ..\_01_BSW\Src\CanTp\CanTp.c	  7125                      PaddingLength is calculated by CanTp_Util_PaddingLength and either equals lFCFrameData.SduLength
